AI assistance used
Claude (Anthropic) was used to:
Draft the initial interactive HTML/CSS/JS
demo ( index.html ) implementing a toy
recurrent-latent-reasoning algorithm (iterative
Bayesian-style hypothesis refinement over a
small grid-transformation puzzle).
Retrieve and verify primary-source details
from the BDH and BDH-CQ arXiv papers
directly (arXiv:2509.26507,
arXiv:2608.09888), rather than from memory
or secondhand blog summaries.

No additional AI tools were used beyond Claude
(Anthropic) as described above.

What a human on the team verified
and can defend
The toy algorithm's logic (hypothesis-space
construction, softmax-sharpening update rule)
was reviewed by team root16 (Swapnil Sarkar,
Swarnabhra Mitra, Mainak Roy), who can explain
live why accuracy should rise as iteration count
increases.
The BDH-CQ numbers (150M parameters; 29.5%
pass@2 / 24.25% pass@1 on public ARC-AGI-1;
~$0.00070/task; LOW/MEDIUM/HIGH effort
results of 21% / 27% / 29.5% pass@2) were
verified against the primary paper by team root16
(Swapnil Sarkar, Swarnabhra Mitra, Mainak Roy).
The three supporting citations (Hao et al. 2024,
Geiping et al. 2025, Saunshi et al. 2025) were
verified against arXiv directly by team root16
(Swapnil Sarkar, Swarnabhra Mitra, Mainak Roy).
What is real vs. illustrative in the
artifact
Live/real: the hypothesis-scoring and iterative
belief-sharpening computation in index.html

runs in the browser on every interaction — it is not
a scripted animation. Moving the effort slider
genuinely recomputes the model's belief
distribution and re-applies it to the query grid.
Illustrative, clearly labeled in-page: the "verbal

chain-of-thought" text panel is a static, hand-
written illustration of what a token-based

reasoner's trace would look like on the same task
— it is not generated live and is labeled as such
directly in the UI.
Not included / explicitly disclaimed: this project
does not run, fine-tune, or reproduce the actual
BDH-CQ model or checkpoint. All BDH-CQ
numbers shown are reference values taken from
the published paper, displayed for comparison —
never presented as live output of our toy model.
